    "type": "question",
    "label": "41",
    "prompt": "Let $a$ and $b$ be rational numbers such that\n$$(2-\\sqrt2)^4=a+b\\sqrt2.$$\nFind the value of $a+b$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$20$",
      "worked": "Treat the second term as $-\\sqrt2$ and use Pascal coefficients $1,4,6,4,1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(2-\\sqrt2)^4&=16-32\\sqrt2+48-16\\sqrt2+4\\\\(2-\\sqrt2)^4&=68-48\\sqrt2\\end{align*}$$\nThus $a=68$ and $b=-48$.\n$$\\begin{align*}a+b&=68-48\\\\a+b&=20\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 52
  },
